#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096324 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Radical Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fcdb2c8-71ca-5bfa-b7fe-49f8f2c05bbb" :question/math-academy-id "e-182" :question/problem "Given that $y = \\sqrt{1-x^2}$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x}\n$$\n\nHere, we've used $u$ instead of $g$ for the intermediate variable.\n\nLet $u=1-x^2$. Then\n\n$$\ny = \\sqrt u = u^{1/2}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = \\dfrac{1}{2}u^{-1/2} = \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt u}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -2x\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} \\cdot (-2x) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2x}{2\\sqrt{u}} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Radical Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f261db81-a459-51b2-a6ff-6738ddf27ce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-6x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244539} {:answer/id #uuid "b49f1c47-c5b2-5898-a141-252c0dd9f49f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{3-6x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244540} {:answer/id #uuid "8ba7fb2e-9930-584f-936d-8d9299d1fcca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12\\sqrt{3-6x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244541} {:answer/id #uuid "f322aba6-1fbc-5c83-98ec-7a682b518644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3-6x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244542} {:answer/id #uuid "0bb46c65-569c-5130-b09b-f4d548d0108e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3-6x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f261db81-a459-51b2-a6ff-6738ddf27ce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-6x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244539} :answer-field/id #uuid "da1e4f69-116a-51a5-b38d-526b338808f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244538}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6fbc1a64-7e7b-5925-877b-d842ceed3e27" :question/math-academy-id "q-107291" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\sqrt{3-6x},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3-6x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}={u}^{1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-1/2}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-6.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-6x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247745 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Radical Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6f4b802-aef0-57ce-8c54-825536e1090f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247747} {:answer/id #uuid "05322057-8b0e-56bb-81ec-0970aa594e51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247748} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1a260e-a31b-5401-9a89-2e7d9261b893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247749} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfc82f7-0ca2-5268-bdae-7aa98b4b447d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247750} {:answer/id #uuid "c5aa7d8b-faf1-5256-bf64-f931a0790b86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d1a260e-a31b-5401-9a89-2e7d9261b893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247749} :answer-field/id #uuid "4271b4ea-d411-5043-8d9d-17669ba4688e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247746}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d088e2f4-98bd-51ca-b324-ad0066961fab" :question/math-academy-id "q-107360" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{1-4x}$ at the point where $x=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=1-4x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-4x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=-2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-2} & ={(-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-4x}})|}_{x=-2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-4(-2)}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Radical Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c76e134d-97f0-52ae-81e0-08ec088bdec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x+7)^3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244560} {:answer/id #uuid "fa95c1d6-3469-51b6-ac2b-ba7ab164518b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x+7)^3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa95c1d6-3469-51b6-ac2b-ba7ab164518b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x+7)^3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244561} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d72aba1-a4a8-5bcd-9a5c-71653263fc1c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244559}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01d86967-f170-52eb-884c-faade3aec8eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-314194" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+7}}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2x+7.$ Then $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}={u}^{-1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x+7{)}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Radical Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce307e5-e22e-5d90-96e6-f0348515a033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{x^2-6x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247754} {:answer/id #uuid "84308f97-9abd-5b9d-913b-85c40ca9e5a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ce307e5-e22e-5d90-96e6-f0348515a033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{x^2-6x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247754} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ce5253c-a2dd-5405-ae23-b94286e309cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247753}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7df4d434-8d33-5d38-aa4e-4d3877f594d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-342680" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u={x}^{2}-6x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x-6.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (2x-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x-3)}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244569 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Radical Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5182c3ce-69e9-54b7-8ca0-bdfb0cf46ea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3x+6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5182c3ce-69e9-54b7-8ca0-bdfb0cf46ea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3x+6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244571} :answer-field/id #uuid "94580e65-33b1-57e3-b860-a15cceb7db2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244570}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d81a556c-ff67-59a3-a319-5cc4ee47cadf" :question/math-academy-id "q-342683" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\sqrt{3x+6}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3x+6.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3x+6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Radical Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cc49d45-6162-51f3-8a8e-bd0382d5fa13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2(5x+1)\\sqrt{5x+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cc49d45-6162-51f3-8a8e-bd0382d5fa13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2(5x+1)\\sqrt{5x+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247758} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec56b9fd-282c-517f-b467-4c1ed9b89331" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247757}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f410e62b-fbc6-55dc-baa4-c0ee039c46d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-342764" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5x+1}}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=5x+1.$ Then $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}={u}^{-1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Radical Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e72d69d4-a8d1-5761-8459-d98d546bccdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244574} {:answer/id #uuid "2bdc1950-359f-5541-b420-602c2a526809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bdc1950-359f-5541-b420-602c2a526809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244575} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfae2bb8-1a73-532a-855c-add69030b974" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244573}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e4c4d02-93ce-585f-897c-bbbbeb8472bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-342802" :question/problem "The slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+12x}}$ at the point where $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3{x}^{2}+12x.$ Then $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}={u}^{-1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x+12.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\cdot (6x+12) \\\\  & =-\\frac{6x+12}{2\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+12x{)}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(-\\frac{6x+12}{2\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+12x{)}^{3}}})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6(2)+12}{2\\sqrt{(3(2{)}^{2}+12(2){)}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{24}{2\\sqrt{{36}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Radical Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c720d59-e194-5266-b56a-c466a517a985" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5x - 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095384} {:answer/id #uuid "f0193492-5011-5859-a30f-bbc8de469e22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x - 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095385} {:answer/id #uuid "0fb017af-74fd-54ab-b3e7-3cf1930e878c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5x - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095386} {:answer/id #uuid "144cb047-1208-5ac8-84b5-438b8948026c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac1{2\\sqrt{(5x-1)^3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095387} {:answer/id #uuid "628b0cb7-1d47-5296-86cf-7c96168acd76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac5{2\\sqrt{(5x-1)^3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "628b0cb7-1d47-5296-86cf-7c96168acd76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac5{2\\sqrt{(5x-1)^3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095388} :answer-field/id #uuid "8efc3cd7-9913-56b8-a464-cc38a8cdd7e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095383}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "854ec833-4bc0-54f0-9210-c708a9342fef" :question/math-academy-id "q-48730" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for $y = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5x - 1}}$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Write $y=(5x-1)^{-1/2}$. For $x>1/5$, the chain rule gives\n$$y'=-\\frac12(5x-1)^{-3/2}\\cdot5=-\\frac5{2(5x-1)^{3/2}}.$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Radical Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d468059-f4b7-51ec-a214-229418cddeaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{4x - 3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095426} {:answer/id #uuid "ce172954-02de-5948-98e6-063d373c04b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4x - 3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095427} {:answer/id #uuid "dd38fa2b-33de-5df5-aa85-ed357c5eb5e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4x + 3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095428} {:answer/id #uuid "fd120f87-d6a9-56e7-ae4f-db302afd2580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4x + 3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095429} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7778bb-8979-5802-bf93-4a409e6e58b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4x - 3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce172954-02de-5948-98e6-063d373c04b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4x - 3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095427} :answer-field/id #uuid "84ab9969-a822-5aa8-beea-30e48f66c60f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095425}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea97309c-a67a-5e7f-aa97-023276ac6669" :question/math-academy-id "q-48846" :question/problem "Given that $y = \\sqrt{4x - 3}$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Write $y=(4x-3)^{1/2}$. For $x>3/4$,\n$$y'=\\frac12(4x-3)^{-1/2}\\cdot4=\\frac2{\\sqrt{4x-3}}.$$"}]}
